  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1800.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1801.02 Applicability",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1801.02 Applicability. Subject to Env-A 1803, this chapter shall apply to the following:\n\n(a) Any person who owns or operates any facility that has asbestos-containing material (ACM) or regulated asbestos-containing material (RACM) on the premises;\n\n(b) Any person involved in asbestos abatement or disturbance of asbestos at an asbestos disposal site, including, but not limited to, analytical laboratories, consultants, industrial hygienists, supervisors, and workers;\n\n(c) Any source, other than an inactive waste disposal site that ceased operating by July 10, 1981, subject to 40 CFR 61, Subpart M;\n\n(d) Any structure, installation, or building previously subject to this chapter, regardless of its current use or function;\n\n(e) Training, licensure, and certification of persons engaged in:\n\n(1) Asbestos abatement, as defined by RSA 141-E:2, II;\n\n(2) School asbestos abatement planning, as defined by RSA 141-E:2, VIII; and\n\n(3) Activities involving the disturbance of asbestos at asbestos disposal sites, as defined by RSA 141-E:2, III; and\n\n(f) Any person involved in a project with the potential to release asbestos fibers during building maintenance, construction, renovation, demolition, or other similar activities; or processing, transport, and disposal activities.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, Revision Note #2, and Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-A 1800) #14104, eff 11-1-24, EXPIRES: 11-1-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1800.html"
}
